meta {
  name: Ratings
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  The signed-in user's ratings. Each game is scored from 1 to 5 on `experience`, `mechanics`, `replayability`, and
  `enjoyment`; responses add `overall_rating`, the average of the four. Ratings are addressed by the game's
  BoardGameGeek ID. Run **Catalog → Get Game** first so `bggGameId` is in the local catalog.

  The requests below run as a round trip (rate → rate again → list → update → delete), so the folder can be re-run.
}
